there's a whole lot going on in Mortal  Kombat 11 and it can be overwhelming but  we're here to steer you in the right  direction and offer some quick tips to  help you become a savage fighter here  are 12 things you should consider to hit  the ground running do the tutorials and  character lessons NetherRealm Studios  has gone the extra mile by making sure  fighting game beginners and veterans  alike can efficiently learn the ins and  outs of MK 11 thanks to a robust  tutorial not only will you learn about  the different strategies for certain  situations of a match but it will also  walk you through the more complex  fighting game mechanics like the frame  data of movesets  zoning escaping pressure and a whole lot  more study move list data beyond the  tutorial itself each character's inputs  for special moves and combos are  available in the move list with all the  frame data and damage numbers included  this helps pull the curtain on  information traditionally dug up by more  seasoned players like start up speed  recovery time and frame disadvantages  when blocked all that information is  readily available in menus for every  single character's moves  don't waste your fatal blow MK 11 has a  new comeback mechanic called the fatal  blow when you're down 30% health or less  you're granted the opportunity to  perform a fatal blow by pressing both  triggers simultaneously character  animations will vary but if you can land  it the fight will transition to a quick  cinematic style combo that deals  significant damage you're only allowed  to land one per match so use it wisely  and don't waste it on the first round if  you don't think you can realistically  make a comeback fatal blows can also be  blocked so consider using it in a combo  for a guaranteed hit  make use of the offensive and defensive  meters most fighting games have you  building up a meter in order to unleash  special attacks but MK 11 does things a  bit differently by giving you two  separate meters for offense and defense  you start each fight with them full and  they automatically replenish at a fixed  rate amplifying certain attacks expends  the offensive meter which results in  extra damage additional hits or the  opportunity to extend combos performing  breakaways for defense will let you  escape juggles and get back up faster  with a window of invulnerability put  together some combo strings to maximize  your damage output you'll want to learn  how to create combo strings it's routine  for most fighting games and MK 11 equips  you with the knowledge needed to  experiment yourself mechanics like  launch attacks to set up juggling combos  stun attacks to make opponents  vulnerable and amplified attacks to  create windows for extended combos are  the keys to better combos as detailed as  the tutorial is it won't spell out combo  strings for you but it does give you the  tools necessary for executing advanced  combos customize character variations to  your liking MK 11 features more  customization options than previous  games you can pick out your favorite  special moves pieces of gear and stat  changing augments to create your own  variations for characters this allows  you to get creative and combine  different elements of a character's move  set but also tweak how they behave in AI  fights cosmetics aren't tied to stat  changes like injustice to so you can put  all that gear you've gathered to use and  make fighters look the way you want get  familiar with preset variations to play  competitively while you can tinker with  the many aspects of each character when  you make your own custom variations  you're restricted to two predetermined  variations when playing ranked matches  online be sure to use these presets and  study what they're capable of to stay on  top and MK 11s competitive matches the  different currencies and how they work  coins are awarded for pretty much doing  anything in the game you use coins to  open most chests in the crypt which can  grant you cosmetic gear new animations  and moves  flair for your combat card among other  things soul fragments are another type  of currency acquired by winning matches  you can begin spending these once you  obtain airmax  amulet in the crypt which is used to  open green chests or repair the bridge  on the island hearts are another  currency earned by performing fatalities  and brutalities in matches these will  let you open another type of special  chests in the crypt towers of time  challenges and crypt chests also reward  you with these currencies to help  accelerate the process time crystals are  a form of premium currency that can  either be purchased or earned in  specific challenges these allow you to  straight up buy things in the premium  shop like character skins and new intro  or taunt animations as it stands the  price of items in the store makes it  fairly difficult to buy things by solely  grinding for time crystals use our crypt  guide the Crypt has changed quite a bit  this time around it's now a sort of  third-person adventure mode where you  explore Shang Tsung's Island solve  puzzles and spend in-game currency to  open chests that unlock extra content  longtime fans will also come across  plenty of references and easter eggs  while exploring like Goro's dining room  in mataró x' horn grind at the towers of  time at the end of the day the towers of  time is the most efficient place to  grind for currency and obtained gear  towers consist of a series of fights  with specific sometimes wacky conditions  and modifiers you won't see anywhere  else in the game for example you might  have to win two rounds in a match while  your opponent only needs to win one or  missiles will randomly shoot at you  throughout the match and deal  unblockable damage modifiers widely vary  some of which might be frustrating to  deal with this is also where you use  consumables which are a variety of stat  boosts or attacks you can summon to give  you an edge or even the playing field in  the more challenging towers if you find  the towers of time to be more on the  frustrating side then we suggest sending  in an AI Ally to do the fighting for you  daily challenges are another way to get  currency when you pull up your combat  card in the main menu you can see a set  of daily challenges on the left so far  these have been fairly simple tasks like  winning a certain number of matches with  a specific character regardless of  difficulty and opponent  completing these challenges reward you  with in-game currency like a decent  chunk of coins story mode is great  and gets you a good amount of coins do  it MK 11 story mode brings you into the  series's lor with self serious yet  ridiculously fun cutscenes and player  driven fights  you'll get acquainted with most of the  games roster and their backstories  throughout the story modes twelve  chapters in addition to being a wildly  entertaining ride with a ton of great  moments for a longtime fans and  newcomers alike  the story mode awards you with a lot of  coins and some cosmetic items to get you  started on the customization process  what else would you recommend when  starting up MK 11 let us know in the  comments below and thanks for watching
 

